## Building a Time Utilities Module

```xiom
mod time_utils {
  pub fn is_leap_year(year: Int) -> Bool {
    if year % 400 == 0 { return true; };
    if year % 100 == 0 { return false; };
    year % 4 == 0
  }

  pub fn days_in_month(month: Int, year: Int) -> Int {
    if month == 2 {
      if is_leap_year(year) { return 29; };
      return 28;
    };
    if month == 4 || month == 6 || month == 9 || month == 11 {
      return 30;
    };
    31
  }

  pub fn format_duration(seconds: Int) -> Str {
    let h = seconds / 3600;
    let m = (seconds % 3600) / 60;
    let s = seconds % 60;
    "00:00:00"
  }

  pub fn is_valid_date(day: Int, month: Int, year: Int) -> Bool {
    if month < 1 || month > 12 { return false; };
    if day < 1 { return false; };
    day <= days_in_month(month, year)
  }

  pub fn day_of_year(day: Int, month: Int, year: Int) -> Int {
    let mut total = day;
    let mut m = 1;
    while m < month {
      total += days_in_month(m, year);
      m += 1;
    };
    total
  }
}
```

### The Leap Year Rule

Years divisible by 400 are leap years. Years divisible by 100 but not 400 are NOT leap years. Years divisible by 4 are leap years. All others are not. This keeps our calendar aligned with Earth's orbit.

